      "title": "The invasion of Poland",
      "time": "1 September – 6 October 1939",
      "durationSec": 11,
      "narration": "Germany invades Poland on 1 September, Bock's army group from the north and Rundstedt's from the south with the Luftwaffe overhead; Britain and France declare war on 3 September but do little in the west. Under the Nazi–Soviet pact the Red Army invades from the east on 17 September. Warsaw surrenders on 27 September and the last Polish forces on 6 October: some 66,000–70,000 Polish soldiers are killed and about 700,000 captured by the Germans.",
