      "title": "The fall of France and Dunkirk",
      "time": "10 May – 25 June 1940",
      "durationSec": 13,
      "narration": "Bock's Army Group B draws the Allies into Belgium and the Netherlands while Rundstedt's Army Group A, with Guderian's and Kleist's panzers, comes through the Ardennes and crosses the Meuse at Sedan on 13 May, then races to the Channel and cuts the Allied armies in two. About 338,000 British and French troops are evacuated from Dunkirk by 4 June. Italy declares war on 10 June, Paris falls on 14 June and France signs an armistice on 22 June; nearly 1.8 million Allied soldiers are taken prisoner.",
