    {
      "id": "p4",
      "title": "The Battle of Britain",
      "time": "10 July – 31 October 1940",
      "durationSec": 11,
      "narration": "To clear the way for an invasion, Göring's Luftflotten attack the Channel convoys, then the RAF's airfields, then London. Dowding's Fighter Command, directed by radar and the Observer Corps, keeps enough Hurricanes and Spitfires in the air to deny the Luftwaffe control of the sky: the RAF loses about 1,744 aircraft, the Luftwaffe about 1,977. The night Blitz on British cities begins on 7 September, and Hitler puts off the invasion indefinitely.",
